<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="weapons">Weapons and Offhands for Shadow Priest DPS Phase 4</h2>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="main-hand-weapons-for-shadow-priest-dps-phase-4">Main Hand Weapons for Shadow Priest DPS Phase 4</h4>Who knew the Lich King was actually 17 different weapons in a trenchcoat? Being the final boss, his drops are obviously going to be the best choice. The gap between <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50734/royal-scepter-of-terenas-ii">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_115.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Royal Scepter of Terenas II</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50608/frozen-bonespike">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_101.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frozen Bonespike</span></a> is bigger than any other option, but it comes with the struggle of competition. The Lich King drops everyones BiS weapons, so you're going to have to fight.<br/>
